      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-143473",
      ":question/problem": "Suppose $X_{1}, X_{2}, X_{3}$ is an I.I.D random sample with $X_{i}\u223cPo(\u03b8)$ with unknown rate parameter $\u03b8$. You're given the particular sample\n$x_{1} = 3, x_{2} = 4, x_{3} = 2$.\nThe log-likelihood function of the sample is given by\n$l(\u03b8) = a\u03b8 + b\\ln \u03b8 - \\ln c$.\n\nFind the value of $a + b + c$.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
